NNAAMMEE
       fsfreeze - suspend access to a filesystem (Ext3/4, ReiserFS, JFS, XFS)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ffssffrreeeezzee ----ffrreeeezzee|----uunnffrreeeezzee _m_o_u_n_t_p_o_i_n_t

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffssffrreeeezzee suspends or resumes access to a filesystem.

       ffssffrreeeezzee halts any new access to the filesystem and creates a stable
       image on disk. ffssffrreeeezzee is intended to be used with hardware RAID
       devices that support the creation of snapshots.

       ffssffrreeeezzee is unnecessary for ddeevviiccee--mmaappppeerr devices. The device-mapper
       (and LVM) automatically freezes a filesystem on the device when a
       snapshot creation is requested. For more details see the ddmmsseettuupp(8) man
       page.

       The _m_o_u_n_t_p_o_i_n_t argument is the pathname of the directory where the
       filesystem is mounted. The filesystem must be mounted to be frozen (see
       mmoouunntt(8)).

       Note that access-time updates are also suspended if the filesystem is
       mounted with the traditional atime behavior (mount option ssttrriiccttaattiimmee,
       for more details see mmoouunntt(8)).

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --ff, ----ffrreeeezzee
           This option requests the specified filesystem to be frozen from new
           modifications. When this is selected, all ongoing transactions in
           the filesystem are allowed to complete, new wwrriittee(2) system calls
           are halted, other calls which modify the filesystem are halted, and
           all dirty data, metadata, and log information are written to disk.
           Any process attempting to write to the frozen filesystem will block
           waiting for the filesystem to be unfrozen.

           Note that even after freezing, the on-disk filesystem can contain
           information on files that are still in the process of unlinking.
           These files will not be unlinked until the filesystem is unfrozen
           or a clean mount of the snapshot is complete.

       --uu, ----uunnffrreeeezzee
           This option is used to un-freeze the filesystem and allow
           operations to continue. Any filesystem modifications that were
           blocked by the freeze are unblocked and allowed to complete.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

FFIILLEESSYYSSTTEEMM SSUUPPPPOORRTT
       This command will work only if filesystem supports has support for
       freezing. List of these filesystems include (2016-12-18) bbttrrffss,
       eexxtt22//33//44, ff22ffss, jjffss, nniillffss22, rreeiisseerrffss, and xxffss. Previous list may be
       incomplete, as more filesystems get support. If in doubt easiest way to
       know if a filesystem has support is create a small loopback mount and
       test freezing it.

